# GitHub push after major changes

This repo is https://github.com/krabhi75/LIAA (branch `main`). Push to origin only — that remote is LIAA, not aetherclose.

After a **major** change set (new feature, UI overhaul, Agora/MCP fix, demo-readiness work):

1. Commit with a concise why-focused message. Do not commit `.env.local` or secrets.
2. **Push to `origin` immediately** (`git push -u origin HEAD` if the branch has no upstream).
3. Do not force-push `main`.
4. Skip empty commits.

Minor copy tweaks do not need a push unless the user asks.
